# Offer a corpse Aiswin does not want, at an altar of Aiswin.
# Oracle for inc-52b. Run it with tools/check_sacrifice.sh.
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/sacrifice-aiswin.keys 1
#
# WHAT THIS COVERS THAT sacrifice-wildcard.keys DOES NOT. That script proves
# a MA_ALL row can match a corpse. This one proves the rows BELOW the MA_ALL
# rows are reachable at all. They are a different mechanism, and Aiswin is
# the god who uses it.
#
# THE PATH. Aiswin accepts only blood vengeance -- a hostile creature that
# wounded the player before the player killed it. His GODWATCH handler
# (lib/religion.irh:240-248) tags such a creature with CORPSE_FLAG eID=Aiswin.
# At sacrifice time his PRE(EV_SACRIFICE) handler (lib/religion.irh:299-315)
# checks that tag, and when it is absent it sets e.EParam = MA_CHOICE1.
#
# Character::Sacrifice takes the default arm of its switch on e.EParam and
# sets sacType = 125. That DISABLES the isMType branch of the match test,
# because that branch runs only when sacType is -1. So the four MA_SAPIENT
# rows and the two MA_ALL rows can no longer match anything, whatever the
# corpse is. Only a row whose category is literally 125 can match, and in
# Aiswin's list (lib/religion.irh:133-141) that is row 6, MA_CHOICE1
# SAC_UNWORTHY -- which sits BELOW both MA_ALL rows.
#
# The old loop stopped at the first zero in the left slot, and MA_ALL is 0,
# so row 6 was unreachable. sacCat stayed -1 and the player got
# MSG_UNINTERESTED, which is the wrong message: the god is not uninterested,
# he has judged the offering unworthy.
#
# MEASURED 2026-08-18, seed 1, this key script, one line of src/Prayer.cpp
# different between the two builds:
#
#   before: "Aiswin seems uninterested in your offering."
#   after:  "A silky whisper mindspeaks: |Insufficient.|"
#
# WHY THE DWARF CORPSE IS THE RIGHT OFFERING. It is a corpse that was already
# lying on the floor at level generation. The player never fought it, so it
# carries no CORPSE_FLAG, so Aiswin classifies it MA_CHOICE1. That is exactly
# the case this script needs. Do not swap it for a corpse the player killed.
#
# WHY THE PATRON IS NOT AISWIN. chargen.keys makes an orc barbarian, and at
# this seed the game gives him Khasrach. Converting to Aiswin needs a
# devotion quest, which a key script cannot drive. It does not matter here:
# Aiswin's classification and the row matching both ignore who the player
# worships. Praying at another god's altar only adds the god picker below
# and changes the prompt from "abis" to "cas".
#
# SEED-LOCKED, for the same reasons as sacrifice-wildcard.keys: the walk onto
# the dwarf corpse is counted moves, and [w] is that corpse's menu letter.
# tools/check_sacrifice.sh asserts both, and calls a drift INCONCLUSIVE
# rather than FAIL.

@include chargen.keys

END                 # step south-west, off the arrival square
LEFT*5              # ...and west onto the dwarf corpse

w                   # wizard mode -- lowercase, see the SHIFT note in
y                   # Wposix.cpp TokenToKey; 'W' is a different keystroke
M                   # [M] Create Altar
"Aiswin"
ENTER

@dump:altar

p                   # pray; the altar is Aiswin, the patron is Khasrach
1                   # "Pray to [1] Aiswin or [2] Khasrach?" -- take the altar
s                   # prompt is "cas"; [s] sacrifice
@dump:offer         # so the check can prove WHICH corpse [w] is
w                   # [w] dwarf corpse (on floor)

@dump:sacrifice
@quit
